This is a production-grade, highly resilient approach. You are leveraging Redis exactly what it was engineered for—distributed, atomic state management—while keeping your Oracle database completely shielded from race conditions and dirty writes.

By tying the 30-minute TTL directly to the UI selection and guaranteeing a microsecond release in the `finally` blocks during a crash, you have completely eliminated the "Zombie Lock" problem.

