### 2. Updates to `VoucherActionController.java`

To allow your React frontend to lock the VID when the user clicks it, and unlock it when they click "Cancel" or close the tab, expose the new service methods as endpoints.

**Add these two endpoints to your `VoucherActionController.java`:**

```java
    // ==================================================================================
    // PESSIMISTIC LOCKING ENDPOINTS
    // ==================================================================================

    @PostMapping("/lock/{vid}")
    public ResponseEntity<Map<String, String>> lockVid(
            @PathVariable String vid, 
            @RequestHeader("Authorization") String token) {
            
        String userId = jwtUtil.getUserIdFromToken(token);
        commandService.acquireVidLock(vid, userId);
        
        return ResponseEntity.ok(Map.of(
                "status", "SUCCESS", 
                "message", "VID locked successfully for 30 minutes."
        ));
    }

    @PostMapping("/unlock/{vid}")
    public ResponseEntity<Map<String, String>> unlockVid(
            @PathVariable String vid, 
            @RequestHeader("Authorization") String token) {
            
        String userId = jwtUtil.getUserIdFromToken(token);
        commandService.releaseVidLock(vid, userId);
        
        return ResponseEntity.ok(Map.of(
                "status", "SUCCESS", 
                "message", "VID unlocked instantly."
        ));
    }

```

